    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the $4.50 cancellation fee is refunded in full to the rider, with no driver compensation. This was an advance booking. The record shows the trip was scheduled for 17:55:08 and the rider cancelled at 17:35:08, exactly 1,200 seconds before the scheduled pickup. The platform policy in force sets an advance grace of 900 seconds (platform_policy.advance_grace_before_scheduled_sec = 900). Because the cancellation came more than 900 seconds before the scheduled time, POL-NS-10(b) makes it non-chargeable; POL-NS-10(c) then requires the fee charged on it to be refunded in full with no driver compensation. The driver's argument that POL-NS-10(f) makes the fee chargeable is rejected: limb (f) applies only to a rider cancellation after the grace in limb (a) or limb (b), and this cancellation came before the advance-booking window rather than after it, so limb (b) governs. The driver's performance — accepting at 17:10:08, starting en route at 17:10:16, and a continuous 157-fix trace with no gaps — is accepted, but it cannot make chargeable a fee that the advance-grace rule removes. Independently, the no-show charge fails under POL-NS-01: there is no driver 'arrived' event (arrived_at is null), and the cancellation reason code RIDER_CANCELLED is not one of the three codes POL-NS-01(d) recognises. POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 also support the refund: the trace places the driver about 13,999.99 m from the pickup pin at closest, moving at 57–63 km/h, with 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes and 0.0 seconds of in-geofence dwell against the 180-second free waiting period — a 180-second shortfall. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02738-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) is not used to carry any deciding fact; it is cited only to confirm that POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is unavailable, so it does not lower confidence in this ruling. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-01 is not satisfied, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below 4, and 2/90 = 0.022, below 0.08), so no POL-NS-09(d) escalation arises. The fare figure of $4.50 reconciles with the platform's net cancellation fee, so no POL-NS-08(d) defect arises. The single rider-position fix at 17:35:48 is consistent with the rider being near the pin, but the refund does not depend on it. Confidence is 0.95 because the deciding facts — the scheduled and cancellation timestamps and the fee — are carried by artifacts at weight 1.0. The monetary effect, $4.50, is below the $8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue subject to the appeal route in POL-GEN-04. No referral is issued because no clause that produces one fires."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

