    "explanation": "To the rider: the $4.50 cancellation fee charged on this advance booking is refunded in full. The trip record shows you were matched at 17:10:08 and the pickup was scheduled for 17:55:08; you cancelled at 17:35:08, exactly 1,200 seconds before the scheduled time. POL-NS-10(b) makes a scheduled-trip cancellation made more than the advance grace before scheduled_at (900 seconds in force for this trip, i.e. any cancellation before 17:40:08) non-chargeable whatever the driver's position, and it cannot be shortened by the driver's early dispatch. POL-NS-10(c) then refunds the fee in full with no driver compensation. The 180-second post-match grace in limb (a) gives you nothing (your cancellation was 1,500 seconds after the match), but on a scheduled booking limb (b), not limb (a), is the governing grace, and you cancelled inside it.\n\nTo the driver: I have read your arguments. The $4.50 is not chargeable. Your limb (f) argument is rejected: limb (f) makes a rider's own cancellation chargeable only 'after the grace in limb (a) or (b)', and this cancellation fell inside limb (b)'s protected window rather than after it. Limb (b) is a charging rule in its own right for scheduled trips and is not emptied by limb (f). I accept your factual points - you began moving toward the pickup at 17:10:16, your trace ran 157 fixes with no gaps and 100% coverage, no vehicle/driver mismatch or ask-to-cancel is shown - but on a scheduled booking none of those makes the fee chargeable once limb (b) applies. I also accept that the $4.50 line is the platform's own published figure and reconciles to platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect arises; the defect is chargeability, not arithmetic.\n\nThe charge independently fails the no-show tests. POL-NS-01 limb (a) requires a driver 'arrived' event and this record has none (arrived_at is null; the event list is driver_assigned 17:10:08 -> driver_en_route 17:10:16 -> trip_cancelled 17:35:08, with no arrival marker and no wait-timer events), and limb (d) requires termination under RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT, whereas the trip closed as RIDER_CANCELLED by the rider. POL-NS-02 places the driver's closest approach 13,999.99 m from the pin with 0 qualifying in-radius fixes and speeds of 57.0-63.0 km/h through the cancellation; POL-NS-06 measures an in-geofence dwell of 0.0 s against the 180 s free waiting period, a 180 s shortfall. POL-NS-06(i) offers no accumulation route: EV-ADVIS-02738-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and no claim in this ruling relies on it.\n\nNo driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07's payout condition (POL-NS-01 satisfied in full) is not reached, and the anti-farming check does not trip - no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and 2/90 = 0.022 (below 0.08) - so POL-NS-09(d) is not engaged and the fee is refunded rather than held. POL-NS-04 cannot be run (the chat log holds 0 messages, so limbs (a) and (b) cannot be made out) and is not relied on; POL-NS-12 does not apply (arrival marker BUTTON, no platform arrival or wait-timer events).\n\nConfidence: the deciding facts (accepted_at, cancelled_at, scheduled_at) are carried by EV-TRIP-02738 at weight 1.0 and the amount charged by EV-FARE-02738 at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. Confidence is set at 0.95. The monetary effect, $4.50, is below the $8.00 execution threshold of POL-GEN-05 and executes automatically on issue."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
