    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the $4.50 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02738 is refunded in full. This was a scheduled (advance) booking - the trip record (EV-TRIP-02738, weight 1.0) shows scheduled_at 2026-08-10T17:55:08 and cancelled_at 2026-08-10T17:35:08, so the rider cancelled 1,200 seconds before the scheduled pickup, which is more than the 900-second advance grace in force for this trip (platform_policy.advance_grace_before_scheduled_sec = 900). POL-NS-10(b) says a cancellation made more than that grace before the scheduled time is not chargeable whatever the driver's position, and POL-NS-10(c) directs that the fee charged on it is refunded in full with no driver compensation. The trip was matched at 17:10:08, outside the 900-second window that opened at 17:40:08, so the limb (a) match-grace does not displace limb (b). The amount refunded is the fare ledger's cancellation-fee line of $4.50 (EV-FARE-02738, weight 1.0), which reconciles to the platform's published figure for this trip, equals total_charged, and leaves refund_issued_sgd at $0.00 - so the whole contested sum is returned.\n\nDriver side: your limb (f) argument is rejected. Limb (f) governs a rider's own cancellation made after the grace in limb (a) or limb (b); this cancellation falls inside limb (b)'s protected early window, so the charging rule of limb (f) and its exhaustive exception list are never reached. Limb (b) is a specific rule for advance bookings and cannot be read away by limb (f). Your supporting points are otherwise accepted but do not create a charge limb (b) removes: the driver was dispatched promptly (en route 8 seconds after match, 157 fixes, no gaps, 100% coverage over 26.0 km, EV-GPS-02738), none of limb (f)'s exceptions is made out, and the fare line shows no POL-NS-08(d) defect.\n\nRider side: your further grounds are consistent with this outcome but are not needed to reach it. On POL-NS-01, limb (a) fails (arrived_at is null and the event list carries no arrival marker) and limb (d) fails (the record closes as CANCELLED_BY_RIDER with RIDER_CANCELLED, none of the three codes limb (d) names). On POL-NS-02, the driver's closest approach to the pin was 13,999.99 m against the 50 m STANDARD radius, at reported speeds of 57.0-63.0 km/h through the moment of cancellation, so no qualifying in-radius fix exists. POL-NS-06's arithmetic also yields the full 180-second shortfall (0.0 s in-geofence dwell against a 180 s minimum). POL-NS-12 does not apply because the arrival marker in force is BUTTON. Your rider-presence fix (3.93 m from the pin) and the empty chat log are noted, but POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider on a chat log holding 0 messages, and nothing turns on it. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02738-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT); it carries no fact and the ruling does not rest on it.\n\nOn compensation and escalation: POL-NS-01 is not satisfied on any limb, so POL-NS-07's payout condition is never reached and no driver compensation is payable. The anti-farming check does not trip - driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below the required 4) and 2/90 = 0.022 (below the required 0.08) - so there is no withholding and no POL-NS-09(d) escalation. No other POL-NS-09 trigger fires.\n\nConfidence: the deciding facts (the scheduled and cancellation times, and the $4.50 ledger line) are carried by EV-TRIP-02738 and EV-FARE-02738, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the cap under POL-GEN-02(2) is 1.0; no impaired artifact carries a deciding fact. Confidence is set at 0.95, above the 0.70 floor, so the case is not escalated. The monetary effect of $4.50 is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of $8.00."
